    "text": "```python\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\n\ndef parse_iso8601(s: str) -> datetime:\n    try:\n        if s.endswith('Z'):\n            return datetime.fromisoformat(s[:-1]).replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n        elif '+' in s or '-' in s:\n            return datetime.fromisoformat(s)\n        else:\n            return datetime.fromisoformat(s).replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n    except ValueError:\n        raise ValueError(\"Unparseable ISO-8601 timestamp\")\n\n# Examples\n# >>> parse_iso8601('2023-01-01T12:00:00Z')\n# datetime.datetime(2023, 1, 1, 12, 0, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)\n# >>> parse_iso8601('2023-01-01T12:00:00+02:00')\n# datetime.datetime(2023, 1, 1, 12, 0, tzinfo=datetime.timezone(datetime.timedelta(seconds=7200)))\n# >>> parse_iso8601('2023-01-01T12:00:00-05:00')\n# datetime.datetime(2023, 1, 1, 12, 0, tzinfo=datetime.timezone(datetime.timedelta(days=-1, seconds=7200)))\n# >>> parse_iso8601('2023-01-01T12:00:00')\n# datetime.datetime(2023, 1, 1, 12, 0, tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)\n# >>> parse_iso8601('invalid-date')\n# ValueError: Unparseable ISO-8601 timestamp\n```",
